    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0036",
      "sequence": 48,
      "meaning": "By Śambhu’s grace, good understanding blossomed in the heart and the poet Tulsī creates the Rāmacaritamānasa. He makes it beautiful according to his understanding; good people of pure heart, hear it and correct it. Good understanding is the ground, the heart its deep site, Vedas and Purāṇas the ocean, and saints the clouds. They rain excellent water in the form of Rāma’s fair fame—sweet, enchanting and auspicious. The accounts of his embodied play provide the water’s cleanness and remove stain; indescribable loving devotion provides its sweetness and refreshing coolness. This water benefits the rice-crop of merit and is the very life of Rāma’s devotees. Falling upon the soil of intellect, the holy water gathers and flows beautifully along the path of hearing. It fills the excellent Lake of the Mind, settles in a fine place, and remains long—pleasant, cool, delightful and lovely. Reflecting with intelligence, the poet composed four excellent, beautiful dialogues; these are the four enchanting ghāṭs of this lovely sacred lake.",
